      "updated_at": "2020-10-27T11:57:44Z",
      "body": "A lot has happened since these experimental ideas were first proposed earlier in 2020. The UK’s CMA have recommended common personal identifiers as a remedy for competition issues in the [digital online marketplace](https://www.gov.uk/cma-cases/online-platforms-and-digital-advertising-market-study#final-report). Such identifiers will have a significant impact on all proposals and work with privacy as justification. Given this proposal seems to be at least in part solving a problem related to privacy the proposal will be impacted and should be aligned to this broader requirement.\r\n\r\nThe report recognizes the need to maintain existing use cases and features until alternatives are found that create a level playing field. As such this proposal is dependent on defining alternative solutions for all the use cases listed.\r\n\r\nRegulators including the European Commission have identified dominant vertically integrated market participants maintain their dominance by capturing agreement for all products and services at the point of accepting consent for an essential service. Therefore, a dominant player may obtain consent and access to information that is practically denied to their competitors.\r\n\r\nThe TPAC session this afternoon might be an opportunity to discuss this in more detail.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
